      "program_name": "Supportive Housing Development Fund NOFA (SHDF NOFA)",
      "administering_agency": "County of Santa Clara Office of Supportive Housing (OSH)",
      "funding_type": "loan",
      "typical_award_size": "Single over-the-counter solicitation that consolidates all County-controlled housing production funds since 2017 (current NOFA issued August 16, 2021). Sources: 2016 Measure A bond, No Place Like Home (County is an alternative county with a direct allocation of $106,085,749 over four rounds; $102.9 million committed), the $40 million I/DD Housing Fund, Stanford Affordable Housing Fund, HOME (about $1 million a year; $3,269,475 programmed for FY 2026-27), CDBG (site acquisition), PLHA, Local Housing Trust Fund match and Homekey+ (over $40 million awarded in 2025-26 for Algarve Apartments with Abode). Measure A acquisition and predevelopment loans were capped at $8 million.",
      "per_unit_cap": "Not published. Underwriting guidelines are reviewed annually against state and federal capital sources.",
      "affordability_requirement": "Priority on extremely low-income and special needs households: homeless and chronically homeless, seniors, transition-age youth, agricultural workers, persons with disabilities. Since 2015 the County has funded 7,183 units, 2,997 set aside for homeless households.",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "new construction",
        "acquisition-rehab",
        "supportive housing",
        "predevelopment",
        "farmworker housing"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "Over the counter, no fixed deadline. With Measure A nearly committed, new awards depend on program income, NPLH interest, HOME, PLHA and state awards; the County Housing Element lists the SHDF NOFA as ongoing through 2031.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "santaclaracounty.gov subdomains (osh, asr, bhsd, news, files) returned HTTP 403 to automated access on 2026-11-07; records were built from the Board of Supervisors IQM2 legislative files (sccgov.iqm2.com), the County Housing Element, Santa Clara County Housing Authority documents, HCD and BOE pages. The NOFA is the single door for County capital in Santa Clara County; applications are underwritten by OSH and taken to the Board in numbered rounds (Round 14 on May 20, 2025) or as off-cycle items. SCCHA project-based vouchers are awarded alongside County capital, and MTW Activity 2016-2 lets SCCHA attach PBVs without a separate competition to projects selected through the County NOFA within the last 15 years. OSH also manages a County Managed Housing Production Pipeline with the 15 cities and SCCHA, supports applications to CTCAC, CDLAC and HCD, and funded 11 tax credit awards in 2025. The County loan portfolio exceeds $1 billion across more than 12,000 units. Source is the County 2023-2031 Housing Element Program 1.01, supplemented by the March 17, 2026 HLUET annual report (sccgov.iqm2.com/Citizens/Detail_LegiFile.aspx?ID=127742) and the October 20, 2026 funding commitments item (ID=130362).",
